Z||000000||85fierose||02-24-2000||08:48 PM||||Just a quick question...what are the largest diamater tires any of you have tried to put on a fiero. Also did you have to use custom rims or were you able to match the lug pattern from another vechile. Is there a simple measurment i could take to find the maximum size?||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||09:14 PM||||Just sold my 17s was running 245/40 on the rear and 215/40 on the front.. have 18s now and no tires.. ran out of money...  as for equasion to figure out what will work...<P>tire width*aspect ratio/25.4*2+wheel diameter this will tell you how far off your speed o will be.  as for if you wondering what the widest tire to fit a given rim.. well width/25.4-wheel width/2   ( 225-50-15 on a 15x6)   225/25.4=8.85  8.85-6/2=1.4 this leave 1.4" on BOTH sides of the tire un supported by the rim. Not extremely unsafe but not all that great either.. try to kee it as close to .5 as possible but 1" is ok. that from pirelli and toyo||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||09:21 PM||||sorry for the math lesson... i had 17x7 42mm offset (front) (bolt pattern 5x100mm) 17x8.5 40mm offset (rear) as for other cars.. uuum Cavalier Z24 (95 or newer) 16" wheels, Many Chrysler cars had this same bolt pattern. uuum the Baretta GTZ had 16" wheels a few differen styls if i remember.. they will all fit fine.  <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>   they can help more too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||85fierose||02-25-2000||12:49 AM||||hey thanks alot! i'll check it out and let you know what i come up with.||||reg||14
